   "body": "# PR review\n\nThe fix is correct and low-risk: the removed guard early-returned during change revalidation whenever another validity key co-occurred with `valueMissing`, and since `customError` is the only key that can realistically co-occur with an empty value, it left `Field.Validity` on stale data (old value, `valueMissing: false`) after a required field was cleared following a custom error. Falling through publishes the fresh native state while `validate` stays deferred (the `element.validationMessage` branch skips it when not validating on change). Nothing here is merge-blocking; the only actionable item is a test-coverage gap the rewrite introduced.\n\n## Tests (1)\n\n### 1. \ud83d\udfe1 Boundary-phase assertions were dropped, leaving the \"deferred custom validation\" half of the contract unpinned\n\n**Location:** `packages/react/src/field/validity/FieldValidity.test.tsx:48`\n\n```tsx\nfireEvent.focus(input);\nfireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: '' } });\n\nexpect(handleValidity.mock.lastCall?.[0].value).toBe('');\nexpect(handleValidity.mock.lastCall?.[0].validity.customError).toBe(true);\nexpect(handleValidity.mock.lastCall?.[0].validity.valueMissing).toBe(true);\n```\n\nThe old test fired the blur/submit boundary after clearing and asserted the full validity publication there. The rewrite asserts only the immediate on-change state and ends, so no test verifies the second half of the new comment in `useFieldValidation.ts` (\"Full custom validation still waits for its boundary\") for this scenario \u2014 i.e. that `validate` is not invoked during the change revalidation but still runs and republishes at the configured boundary.\n\n**Failure scenario:** A future change that starts invoking `validate` during the revalidation fall-through (or breaks the boundary republication after it) would pass this suite unnoticed.\n\n**Fix:** After the immediate assertions, fire the boundary (`fireEvent.blur(input)` / submit click, reusing the existing `validationMode` loop) and assert the published state there; optionally also assert `validate` wasn't called an extra time during the change.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Approve after nits** \u2014 the fix itself is verified correct; only the deferred-validation boundary lost its test coverage.\n\n---\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Review generated with Claude Code\n",
