   "body": "# PR review\n\nThe fix is correct and well-scoped: the change-revalidation guard now lets a stale `customError` coexist with `valueMissing` and falls through to publish the native state immediately, while custom validation stays deferred (the `validationMessage`/`!isValidatingOnChange` branch skips `validate`, pinned by the new `toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` assertions). Other native errors (`badInput`, `typeMismatch`, \u2026) are still deferred, covered by the new Chromium test. One minor, non-blocking edge case found; nothing merge-blocking. Review ran at `low` effort (bugs only).\n\n## Bugs (1)\n\n### 1. \ud83d\udfe1 Array custom errors collapse to one newline-joined string during the revalidation window\n\n**Location:** `packages/react/src/field/root/useFieldValidation.ts:246`\n\n```tsx\nif (element && element.validationMessage && !isValidatingOnChange) {\n  defaultValidationMessage = element.validationMessage;\n  validationErrors = [element.validationMessage];\n```\n\nWhen `validate` returns an array (e.g. `['Too short', 'Needs a digit']`), `setCustomValidity(result.join('\\n'))` stores them joined. The newly reachable fall-through republishes via `element.validationMessage`, so `errors` becomes `['Too short\\nNeeds a digit']` (one item) and `error` the joined string. Previously this path returned early, so the published data kept the original array until the blur/submit boundary re-ran `validate`.\n\n**Failure scenario:** A required field with an array-returning `validate` shows its errors as a `<ul>` in a bare `<Field.Error />` (it renders a list only when `validityData.errors.length > 1`). After the custom errors are set and the user clears the field, the list collapses into a single blob with a literal newline (rendered as a space) until the next blur/submit restores the array.\n\n**Fix:** In the revalidate fall-through, preserve the existing `validityData.errors`/`error` for the custom-error portion instead of re-deriving them from `validationMessage` \u2014 or split `validationMessage` on `'\\n'` when populating `validationErrors`.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Approve after nits** - the regression fix is correct; the only finding is a narrow cosmetic edge case with multi-error custom validators during the revalidation window.\n\n---\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Review generated with Claude Code\n",
